  "title": "Louis S NDE 6960",
  "date": "1984",
  "content": "I just had been eating something. It was about 13:30 hrs. We decided to play astronauts by doing a series of physical exercises: 10 very fast flexings, 10 very fast push-ups, then breathing very fast and emptying the lungs at the most, and turning around 20 times. Then we stopped at the spot and stopped breathing at the same time, for as long as possible. There I just remember being in a dark tunnel with a light at the end. I see my father, who died 4 years ago and who tells me ‘it's not your hour’. I sense the light as being filled with love and it is taking away all the frustrations of my life. I'm obeying my father and turn around, while being sad to leave him again, and happy having seen him. I have to signal here that I had a premonitory dream of his death 72 hours before it happened and had told him so at the time. I woke up stretched out on the tarmac of the covered playground. Nobody seemed to be very anxious about this and it took only a few minutes, as I was told. The incident remained between us, the pupils of our college.",
